  "title": "Provider-neutral work tracker seam with a GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a new `work_tracker` module defining the provider-neutral seam between the factory and a work tracker: the `WorkTracker` trait and its data types, the 'Ready' dispatch rule, the run-finishing write sequence, and an in-memory test double. Alongside it lands the first adapter, `github_work_tracker`, which drives GitHub Issues and Projects v2 through the `gh` CLI — pure argv/payload builders and pure response parsers wrapped in a thin loop over a `GhRunner` trait, with a real runner that enforces a timeout and refuses writes without an explicit token identity.",
